iability:** ICC=0.919 overall; linguistic ICC ~0.98 vs specification ICC ~0.84\n- **DeBERTa classifier PoC:** Binary F1=0.81, inverse danger-detectability relationship\n\n## Experiment design reference (what was planned)\nThe full experiment plan included these experiments:\n1. Clause generation: 300 pairs (50/type × 6), Chantree-style validation, 98% pass\n2. Mini-pilot: 20 episodes validating auth_scope and coreferential\n3. Full API study: 1,800 episodes (3 API models × 300 × 2)\n4. Full open-source study: 1,200 episodes (2 models × 300 × 2)  \n5. Full statistical analysis with all 5 claims\n6. Error analysis: 300 traces, 4 failure modes\n7. Reliability test: 360 episodes, ICC analysis\n8. Realism validation: KS tests vs DRIP-R\n9. Judge calibration: 100 episodes, human annotation\n10. Perturbation control: 300 episodes\n11. SOPBench cross-benchmark: 1,000 episodes\n12. DeBERTa classifier PoC\n\n## Your task\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n1. **Experimental design soundness** — Is the matched-pair design well-executed? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical methodology** — Are the tests appropriate? Effect sizes properly reported? Multiple comparisons handled?\n3. **Measurement validity** — Judge calibration, reliability, ecological validity\n4. **Completeness** — Are claimed experiments all present? Any missing from the plan?\n5. **Reproducibility** — Could someone replicate this? Are details sufficient?\n6. **Weaknesses and concerns** — What are the methodological gaps?\n\n## Output format\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary of contributions (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (numbered, with evidence)\n\n### Weaknesses (numbered, with evidence, severity: major/minor)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n\n### Missing Experiments (comparing paper to plan)\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5  \n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Overall Assessment: X.X (use ARR half-point scale)\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n\nBe rigorous and calibrated.